From e3ac6669ea0e8b0f623c47087cfb8db1f448a8cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:14:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] analysis/rivers.jl: JRA55 river and iceberg water delivered
 to the model ocean, by river, region and month, and where it lands
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The four-month runs are too salty in strips along the river-fed coasts with fresher water just offshore, and the BSO
inflow is too salty. The 16 Nov check (nested/rivers_and_straits.jl) found every JRA55 river near the domain
delivered; this redoes it for the current set-up (the run's own grid, the same JRA55PrescribedLand call as
panarctic.jl, CPU), over the whole run by month, and adds where the water lands: NumericalEarth's routing spreads each
mouth's discharge equally over every wet cell within 1.2° (about 130 km) of its landing cell. rivers.md (by river,
by model region, and each river's distance from its mouth and from the coast, and the part within 30 km of the coast)
and rivers.png (delivered fresh water; distance from the coast).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
